WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.592 --> 00:00:13.852
Back to Oriva.

2
00:00:18.432 --> 00:00:20.232
One thought they sold coffee machines.

3
00:00:20.672 --> 00:00:21.552
The fifth said something

4
00:00:21.592 --> 00:00:22.592
about fresh.

5
00:00:22.992 --> 00:00:24.272
So buyers compared prices,

6
00:00:24.312 --> 00:00:25.912
and the supermarket won.

7
00:00:26.232 --> 00:00:27.192
The founders’ fix?

8
00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:28.272
Say more.

9
00:00:28.492 --> 00:00:29.372
But say everything,

10
00:00:29.412 --> 00:00:30.752
and they remember nothing.

11
00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.449
So which one thing?

12
00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:33.749
Business Strategy

13
00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:34.889
follows the money.

14
00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.321
The founders could talk about

15
00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:38.161
their barista classes for hours.

16
00:00:43.281 --> 00:00:44.821
So the brand leads with beans.

17
00:00:45.241 --> 00:00:46.301
Sorry, classes.

18
00:00:46.859 --> 00:00:48.079
But beans are beans.

19
00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:49.359
Why pay more?

20
00:00:49.779 --> 00:00:50.459
Offer and Value

21
00:00:50.499 --> 00:00:51.919
makes them worth it.

22
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.070
Same price.

23
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:04.910
Now it looks worth it.

24
00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.210
But who’s the hero?

25
00:01:10.426 --> 00:01:11.346
Their first draft

26
00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:13.016
starred Oriva.

27
00:01:13.266 --> 00:01:13.786
Wrong.

28
00:01:13.826 --> 00:01:14.766
The customer is the hero,

29
00:01:14.806 --> 00:01:16.186
with one problem:

30
00:01:16.586 --> 00:01:17.746
which bag do I buy?

31
00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:18.946
Oriva is the guide,

32
00:01:18.986 --> 00:01:20.006
with a plan:

33
00:01:20.466 --> 00:01:22.306
quiz, bag, brew.

34
00:01:22.926 --> 00:01:24.726
Buyers don’t care about your story yet.

35
00:01:24.766 --> 00:01:25.746
They care about theirs.

36
00:01:26.304 --> 00:01:27.804
So where does Oriva stand?

37
00:01:32.084 --> 00:01:33.224
Map every rival:

38
00:01:33.644 --> 00:01:34.324
price across,

39
00:01:34.644 --> 00:01:35.444
freshness up.

40
00:01:40.024 --> 00:01:40.844
He wants in.

41
00:01:41.124 --> 00:01:42.064
She frowns.

42
00:01:42.104 --> 00:01:43.584
A crowd is where you disappear.

43
00:01:43.984 --> 00:01:45.404
She points at the empty corner.

44
00:01:45.624 --> 00:01:46.784
Remember the fifth customer?

45
00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.284
Oriva moves in:

46
00:01:49.564 --> 00:01:50.804
roasted the week you order.

47
00:01:51.084 --> 00:01:52.484
The big rivals can’t match that.

48
00:01:52.524 --> 00:01:53.544
Their beans cross

49
00:01:53.584 --> 00:01:54.504
an ocean first.

50
00:01:54.929 --> 00:01:56.249
But one line only works

51
00:01:56.289 --> 00:01:57.769
if everyone says it.

52
00:01:57.809 --> 00:01:58.929
That’s the Brand Pitch:

53
00:01:59.269 --> 00:02:00.109
the brand out loud,

54
00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:01.409
in three lengths.

55
00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:05.584
Last month,

56
00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:06.704
he pitched the classes,

57
00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:08.624
she pitched the cafés.

58
00:02:08.664 --> 00:02:09.804
Now it’s one pitch,

59
00:02:09.844 --> 00:02:10.684
written down,

60
00:02:10.724 --> 00:02:12.104
so nobody forgets it.

61
00:02:12.144 --> 00:02:13.144
Not even the founders.

62
00:02:13.752 --> 00:02:14.552
Two weeks.

63
00:02:14.912 --> 00:02:16.492
Here’s what Oriva walks out with.

64
00:02:16.805 --> 00:02:18.265
Ask the two founders now.

65
00:02:18.565 --> 00:02:19.245
One answer:

66
00:02:19.465 --> 00:02:21.245
we roast it the week you order.

67
00:02:21.545 --> 00:02:22.745
That’s not a rumour.

68
00:02:22.785 --> 00:02:23.785
That’s a position.

69
00:02:24.305 --> 00:02:25.385
Buyers don’t know it yet.

70
00:02:25.965 --> 00:02:26.275
Notice:

71
00:02:26.315 --> 00:02:27.765
Oriva didn’t say more.

72
00:02:27.805 --> 00:02:28.585
It said less.

73
00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.600
But buyers don’t read strategies.

74
00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:31.860
They read bags.

75
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.860
So how does a bag say fresh?

76
00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.900
That’s Identity.

